 "text": "A glass beaker contains a mass of 0.20kg of water at a temperature of 20°C.\nThe specific heat capacity of water is 4200J/(kg°C).\nA brass block of mass 0.15kg is at a temperature of 170°C. The block is carefully lowered into\nthe beaker of water.\nThe final temperature of both the water and brass is 30°C.\nWhat is the specific heat capacity of the brass?\n(Assume that no water is lost and no thermal energy has been transferred to the beaker or the\nsurroundings.)\nA\n400J/(kg°C)\nB\n660J/(kg°C)\nC\n1200J/(kg°C)\nD\n5600J/(kg°C)",
